Myrmidon Titans were the origin of the the [http://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrmidons Myrmidons], warriors commanded by Achilles in Greek mythology. 

In [[Peru]], Myrmidon was invoked by [[Hoffman]] to attack [[Dante Vale]] and [[Zhalia Moon]]. He was attacked by [[Gar-Ghoul]] but was able to defeat it with help from [[Wilder]]'s [[Weakenshade]] spell. Myrmidon then finished off [[Elf King Oberon]] before being defeated by [[Lok Lambert|Lok's]] [[Baselaird]]. {{Source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Myrmidon was used by Hoffman, alongside a Suit's [[Venomaster]] to fight against Dante's [[Caliban|Powerbonded Caliban]]. After being hit by a misaimed poison attack by Venomaster, Myrmidon was defeated by Caliban. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}

Hoffman later invoked Myrmidon in the underwater ruins of Yonaguni where he and a Suit's [[Shadow Agent]] fought against [[Pendragon|Powerbonded Pendragon]]. He was later joined by [[Wilder]]'s [[Grand Façade]] but they were all knocked backwards when Lok summoned [[Kyojin]], with a huge whirlpool sucking the [[Organization]] and their Titans underwater. {{source|The Guardian of Yonaguni}}
